    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T03:24:53Z",
    "body": "Finding: the culprit is 6cd4f3e01 (merge of #3136). The post-merge run on 5bc0b7129 is green (44977365067). The run on 6cd4f3e01 is red (44977387120) on this one test. The branch of #3136 did not contain #2920, so #3136 did not regenerate `slot_dxf_outline.cl`. The assert is the golden compare (`common/mod.rs:253`, \"golden ... slot_dxf_outline.cl is stale\"). The ends, width and cut box asserts pass. Decision: the code is correct and the golden pinned the old uncut round ends. The new path adds the #2906 wall lap on the 3 mm cutter-centre arcs about (45, 25) and (75, 25). It stays inside the outline, and the stock simulation finds no gouge. I regenerate the golden and add an assert that each round end is cut on its wall arc. Record: `docs/decisions/3278-slot-dxf-golden.md`.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
